            "text": "{\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"If an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee, including employees exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act's (FLSA) requirement to keep records of hours worked (such as bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees defined in 29 CFR part 541), the employer has the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"In order to claim that full-time teachers (as defined in § 825.102) of an elementary or secondary school system, an institution of higher education, or other educational establishment or institution (who often work outside the classroom or at home) are not eligible for FMLA leave, an employer must be able to clearly demonstrate that the teachers did not work 1,250 hours during the previous 12 months.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"background\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Provides a cross-reference directing readers to § 825.801(d) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees, without establishing an independent substantive requirement in this passage.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
